{"record":{"authorityType":"geographicPlaceName","heading":"King's Chapel (Boston, Mass.)","linkCounts":{"subject":1,"totalDescriptions":1},"naId":75646590,"preferred":true,"recordType":"authority","scopeNote":"An 18th-century church located at the corner of Tremont and School Streets in Boston, Massachusetts.  Constructed 1749-1754. Designated a National Historic Landmark on October 9, 1960 and added to the National Register of Historic Places on May 2, 1974.  A location on Boston's Freedom Trail.","sourceNotes":["LC authorities online, Dec. 5, 2017. https://lccn.loc.gov/n85323027","Wikipedia.org, Dec. 5, 2017 (King's Chapel, Boston, Massachusetts) https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/King%27s_Chapel","King's Chapel, Boston, Massachusetts by Stanley Scot, 1939. https://catalog.archives.gov/id/6219819"]}}
